; E1000.EXE's description, for cargo drivers: it goes into the zip as
; E1000.INF (with Source= added) and into CATALOG.TXT as one line per
; [Devices] entry. Raise Version= for every change that is published.
; The devices of the kernel's built-in e1000 driver, which this driver is
; to replace, and the 82544GC (100C), which the built-in never covered.
[Driver]
Name=E1000
Version=1.1.0-1
File=E1000.EXE
Description=Intel PRO/1000 (8254x, 82574L) Ethernet
Licence=MIT
Basic=Yes

[Devices]
8086:100C network
8086:100E network
8086:100F network
8086:1010 network
8086:1011 network
8086:1026 network
8086:1027 network
8086:1076 network
8086:10D3 network
